===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make (products or services) available for [[sale]] and [[promote]] them.
#: {{ux|en|We plan to '''market''' an ecology model by next quarter.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[sell]].
#: {{ux|en|We '''marketed''' more this quarter already than all last year!}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To deal in a market; to buy or sell; to make bargains for provisions or goods.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To shop in a market; to attend a market.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=201|passage=We did a little shopping; but I cannot remember much of the town. It was Saturday night, and all Perth was '''marketing'''.}}

